        "text": "App: Help App View Overview How to use this view Terms and controls Safety and limits App View App: Help application view This image is captured from the live Demo view. Review the current interface before publishing explanatory guidance. Overview Help is the standalone, searchable guide for the Z00Z Wallet Demo. Its menu is built from the _meta.yaml files stored beside the articles, so the visible sections, article order, and available languages follow the checked-in Help content. Opening Help from a screen selects the matching article. Opening Help from the main menu starts here. How to use this view Choose a section in the left menu. On mobile, open the menu button first. Expand a section and select the article for the screen or task you want to understand. Use Search or Ctrl K / ⌘ K to find terms across every article. Change language without losing the selected topic. Follow the article’s safety and availability notes before treating a Demo result as a completed wallet or network operation. Terms and controls Term or control Explanation Contents Metadata-ordered tree containing every published Help article. Search Finds matching article titles and body text in the selected language. Language Changes the Help catalogue while preserving the current topic when that topic exists. App View Screenshot of the Demo screen described by an article. Current topic Article selected by a contextual Help action, search result, or menu link. Safety and limits Help is packaged content; it does not need wallet keys, a wallet session, or private transport data. Screens marked as concept, target, unavailable, or local-only do not prove that a native service executed the described action. Never paste a seed phrase, private key, recovery material, or sensitive message into an issue report or third-party page opened from Help.",
